Consumer endpoints, not contracts
---------------------------------
Several skills call free public endpoints that were never published as APIs
(Google Translate TTS, DuckDuckGo and Bing result pages, free image-generation
sites). These can change, rate-limit or block at any time, and their terms of
service may prohibit automated use. You are responsible for how you use them:

  * keep volume human (the skills are built to be useful, not to be a farm)
  * read the reference/ file of the skill you intend to use commercially
  * do not present outputs as endorsed by the underlying provider

Third-party software you install yourself
-----------------------------------------
install.sh installs or suggests: ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL), poppler (GPL),
Pillow (MIT-CMU), edge-tts (GPL-3.0), piper-tts (MIT) and Piper voice models,
which carry their own licences (most voice datasets are CC BY 4.0 or similar —
check the voice card). None of these are bundled here; nothing is vendored.

Content fetched at runtime
--------------------------
fetch-page and deep-research retrieve third-party pages and quote sentences
from them in reports. Copyright in that text stays with its authors. Citing is
not relicensing: do not redistribute fetched corpora.

